    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nCurrently, the only multicursor information that's given is the data under the `nvim.multicursor`  and `nvim.multicursor.visual` namespaces. But individual cursors have more data than that - #41988 added change marks that are saved for each cursor. I would personally use this for a normal mode version of my rotate-selections mapping, so `qpiw` would get the current word for each cursor, and rotate that word to the next cursor.\n\nOf course, you could simply make a mapping that then cascades to other cursors, where each cursor reads from its own marks - but for something like rotating selections, you need to actually iterate through each cursor and move it to the next one.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThis additional information would be provided to plugins. Maybe in the existing multicursor data with #34683 and #42070, maybe with an explicit function like `nvim_multicursor_get` (proposed [here](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42040#issuecomment-5794708068)).",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
